\abstract(
Study the actual native producer from a tiny, inspectable example through the
retained original experiment and explicit boundary/work controls. Complete
editable C++ programs own every rendered native figure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

A candidate ear must turn counterclockwise in the normalized remaining ring, and
no other remaining vertex may lie on or inside its triangle. The native producer
now validates the complete finite simple boundary and uses exact
stored-coordinate orientation signs for validation and ear tests. It rejects
duplicates, crossings, touches and adjacent backtracking rather than returning a
plausible partial mesh. After each actual clip it retains the actual remaining
original indices. The original seven-vertex concave arrow remains; no external
dataset is needed.

$$ \#\mathrm{triangles}=n-2\quad\text{for a valid simple polygon with }n\ge3. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table reads actual producing records. The native diagram names actual
captured values from that same run.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/polygon_triangulation_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t =
        dm::geometry::triangulate_polygon_trace({{0, 0}, {2, 0}, {2, 2}, {0, 2}});
    std::print("\n| actual ring size | candidate a,b,c | exact turn | actual other-point tests | blocked | " "clipped |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.candidates)
        std::print("| {} | ({},{},{}) | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", r.ring_size,
                   r.triangle.a, r.triangle.b, r.triangle.c, r.orientation,
                   r.containment_tests, r.has_blocker, r.clipped);

    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual normalized initial ring\n{}", t.initial_ring));
    d.node("n1", {9, 0},
           std::format("Actual emitted first ear\n({},{},{})",
                       t.clips[0].triangle.a, t.clips[0].triangle.b,
                       t.clips[0].triangle.c));
    d.node("n2", {18, 0},
           std::format("Actual remaining original ids\n{}", t.clips[0].remaining));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/polygon_triangulation_tiny.svg");
}
```
