> API and interpretation

Every block is a complete editable C++ program. Reusable searches, walks,
geometry decisions, fixture histories and algorithm work live in the canonical
library. Captured records own their values and are not reconstructed by a second
algorithm in the report. Explicit policies count the documented selected calls,
records or scalar entries; they are not peak-byte or wall-clock budgets.
Original reference curves are labelled as references, and finite returned
results are not promoted into universal convergence, recovery, scaling or speed
guarantees.

Independent exact Fraction areas, winding and directed edge-incidence
certificates verify complete meshes for concave, clockwise, collinear-boundary
and full-coordinate-range polygons. Selected predicate counts match
independently counted validation and candidate queries. Frozen comparisons
preserve original triangle-index sequences on three nondegenerate fixtures. The
shared batch passes83 native regression tests,18 directly instrumented sanitizer
tests,84 compiled and executed public examples,391/391 scoped documentation
definitions, standalone and installed header checks, a linked installed consumer
and ten representative symbol hovers. All four complete programs execute and
their computed results and local figures survive HTML and Markdown export. Build
receipts: `build/mepml-conversion/batch-284-293/`.
